      "writtenOn": "2021-04-02T06:34:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "switchPhone is triggered from activate/deactivate requests only that are used for legacy DDS (setDataAllowed). Agree that active flag check on phonestate blocks duplicate setDataAllowed requests.\n\nIssue happens for setPreferredDataModem for which there is no check for active state. And setPreferredDataModem is triggered through sendRilCommands which is called for multiple cases like subid/phoneid change in onEvaluate, Radio cap change etc. This allows multiple setPreferredDataModem requests being sent to RIL.\n\nDuplicate requests are causing problems for temporary DDS switch done for calls on non DDS sub. Also, our automation test scripts which track the request msgs are broken due to this unwanted duplicate requests.",
